Z||000001||mshill||11-22-2000||04:44 PM||||If you are doing a V6 swap (2.8 -&gt; 3.4) you can take all of that off of your 2.8.  When I am done with mine it will look completely stock (and the wiring will be identical) because I am swapping out the complete intake system and valve covers as well.||||reg||1
Z||000002||count_iblis||11-22-2000||05:31 PM||||so basicly i just need the block then?||||reg||1
Z||000003||GarethWright||11-22-2000||08:23 PM||||is it only the 3.4 that you can swap everything from the 2.8? Or can you do that on the 3.8 too?  Also what is a good donor car for the 3.4?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fieroboy1||11-23-2000||07:29 PM||||3.8 is a diff engine, therefore you will not be able to swap components.  A good donor car for the 3.4 is the 93-95 camaro.  My 3.4 is from a 95 camaro with 47,000 miles.  You will need the 3.4 block and i left the 3.4 heads in place, changed the intake to fiero and was able to use stock fiero fuel rail, although i used the 3.4 injectors on the rail.  You will need your 2.8 distributor. I used my stock starter, obviously drilled and tapped on the opposite side.  If you refer to Ed Park's website it has a detailed description of what you have to do. And of course this topic has been been to death with a stick so there a jagillion threads on it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fieroboy1||11-23-2000||07:31 PM||||This is the address for Ed Parks fiero Factory.  VERY HELPFUL!!!!!!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#34" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#34</A> ||||reg||1
